    <node id="LOBOS MARINOS">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> Lobos Marinos are a species of marine mammals that are found in the coastal areas of the southern hemisphere, known for their large size and their ability to adapt to different environments. They are currently listed as a species of least concern by the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN), but they are still threatened by habitat loss, hunting, and pollution. Lobos Marinos are found in the coastal areas of the southern hemisphere, where they live in colonies on rocky shores and in the open ocean. They are well adapted to their environment and can survive in a variety of different habitats. Lobos Marinos are the subject of ongoing research in fields such as biology, ecology, and conservation. Scientists are studying their behavior, habitat preferences, and population dynamics to better understand their role in the marine ecosystem. Lobos Marinos have a complex reproductive cycle that includes a gestation period of up to 12 months, followed by a birth weight of up to 1,000 pounds. They are known to give birth to one calf at a time and nurse their young for up to two years. Lobos Marinos have a complex social behavior that includes hunting, mating, and caring for their young. They are also known for their ability to communicate with each other through vocalizations and body language. Lobos Marinos have several biological characteristics that make them well adapted to their environment, including their large size, their ability to swim and dive, and their thick fur. Lobos marinos son especies de pinn&#237;pedos que se encuentran en las costas atl&#225;nticas y fueguinas de Argentina, conocidos por su adaptaci&#243;n a la vida en el agua y en tierra. Los lobos marinos son un grupo de mam&#237;feros marinos que incluye focas, leones marinos y morsas, conocidos por su adaptaci&#243;n a la vida en el agua y en tierra.</data>
      <data key="d2">047fbbc658a3372904c9003df8fac928,2a07d307a2839ae1f889f579a415bf9a,3e11752f9db0c9d6d3511bebdfdf06fa,c5aabd834197cee0008cbbe12580007f</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
      <data key="d4">0</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">0</data>
      <data key="d7">2c90504bbb6d4e1798f7607a767f22af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PINN&#205;PEDOS">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1">Los pinn&#237;pedos son un grupo de mam&#237;feros marinos que incluye focas, leones marinos y morsas, conocidos por su adaptaci&#243;n a la vida en el agua y en tierra.</data>
      <data key="d2">4637827f6813c74937485d62b3f596b8,9d8e3504b4ee32dcb2cfe65980dddcaa</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
      <data key="d7">e28fb2f565f14b128419d64ec722c2f5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOBOS MARINOS DE UNO Y DOS PELOS">
      <data key="d0">PINNIPED</data>
      <data key="d1"> Los lobos marinos de uno y dos pelos son especies de pinn&#237;pedos that inhabit the coasts of our country, known for their social behavior and their habitat in colonies. They are also known for their distinctive pelage.</data>
      <data key="d2">08e9f4bcb8bee78292601780a46936c6,4637827f6813c74937485d62b3f596b8,583f551deb29bf66f80bcf97f89e3c64,59a2e76fa5cfb51e15d733d19084f125,5a07380f5aada9c6c6ef41f242e1c536,773258f4983ae1adc2e995e6a7bd7aa6,8a0c5d2be39b9a9e02f97cbc7551030c,929b52dcc39f3e79e12fe7e15557dbaf,9d8e3504b4ee32dcb2cfe65980dddcaa,a7319504eeb762ae0cc5b15c4d6b5461,abfbf0cbd4646b7d6aff58787b3de0bd,acce0f2d52d35b868047d606555fc1e4,b58cdc05bb2d9dbcf563d7eaa562cf0f,c189d2e78df197f5464424712ff00b40,cd89fd819728e8bb01132a958eb61182,cf58f0416a8d27360f6d6e772471b831,ff2c7455e99e69b4239b601fef6b447e</data>
