    <node id="ISLOTE SUR DE PUNTA LOBER&#205;A">
      <data key="d0">POPULACI&#211;N DE PING&#220;INOS</data>
      <data key="d1"> ISLOTE SUR DE PUNTA LOBERA is a marine ecosystem located in the southern part of Punta Lobera Island. The island is home to a population of lobos marinos, which are characterized by their size and strength. The lobos marinos on the island are also the subject of conservation efforts, which aim to protect their habitat and ensure their survival. The island's marine ecosystem is also home to a population of penguins, which are known for their distinctive black and white plumage and their ability to swim and fly. The population of penguins on the island is closely monitored by researchers, who study their behavior and ecology to better understand their role in the island's ecosystem. The lobos marinos and penguins on the island also reproduce, with the lobos marinos giving birth to their young in underwater caves and the penguins nesting on the island's rocky shores. The research on the lobos marinos and penguins on the island is ongoing, with scientists working to understand their interactions with each other and with their environment. The topography of the island is also an important factor in the marine ecosystem, with its rocky shores and underwater caves providing habitat for a variety of marine species. Overall, ISLOTE SUR DE PUNTA LOBERA is a unique and important marine ecosystem, home to a diverse range of marine species and providing valuable insights into the complex relationships between them.</data>
      <data key="d2">d12aea8b41f8654da913712b1182332f</data>
      <data key="d5">2</data>
      <data key="d6">43</data>
      <data key="d7">bc22f13e784c42369d7d0d2dd0147a4c</data>
