    <node id="TOPOGRAF&#205;A REGIONAL">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1"> The topography of the regional area of S.W. de la Bah&#237;a Thouctof includes a small island with vegetation, a narrow rocky beach with a little sand, and a resting area. The coast is smooth and is cut by a canyon that extends from S.W. to N.E., and empties onto the coast over a 20-meter-long section. The coast also features high cliffs cut at a steep angle, with abundant rounded rocks and sand in their cavity. The coast of the Gulf of San Jorge includes a rocky beach with small hills that project resting areas, low cliffs with vegetation, and a clayey area with typical vegetation.</data>
      <data key="d2">542231ad71887d5ea52f251bd5ce2e3e,b936698b8bf77875919870e3152faf6d,e411653fa84230bcd9ca8f9b38657cca</data>
