    <node id="LOBER&#205;AS">
      <data key="d0">CONSEJOS MARITIMOS DE TIERRA DEL FUEGO</data>
      <data key="d1"> Lobos marinos are marine mammals that are hunted for their meat and other byproducts in Argentina. The observations made on the different industrialization plants that have concessions for lobos marinos show that the total utilization of the animal is not achieved. Efforts to simultaneously utilize the organs, waste, bones, etc. of lobos marinos, which is successfully practiced in other countries, have not been successful in Argentina due to their anti-economic nature. Temporary tasks are carried out during the hunting season, within the established limits for each concession and within the regulated times. The direction of these tasks is usually under a common regime that is specialized for each stage of the work. The maximum authority is the concessionaire or the substitute in case of an accident. The capataz is the man who knows the work and is usually initiated in the activities as a simple "lobero". The concessionaire deposits his trust in him and is responsible for ordering, disposing, and executing any work that relates to any of the stages inherent to the exploitation. It is worth noting that the capataz is always a man of character and notable ascendancy over the rest of the "comparsa".</data>
      <data key="d2">da6bf576b51c96c74aee885ecd44a5d3</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">67</data>
      <data key="d7">f48fa7d622d541f6a37b8f693f5c36eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSEJOS MARITIMOS DE TIERRA DEL FUEGO">
      <data key="d0">CONSEJOS MARITIMOS DE TIERRA DEL FUEGO</data>
      <data key="d1"> The Consejos Mar&#237;timos de Tierra del Fuego are responsible for managing the fishing industry in the region. However, observations conducted on the different industrial plants that have concessions in the area suggest that the total utilization of the animal is not being achieved. Efforts to simultaneously utilize the organs, residual waste, bones, etc. of the sea lions, which is successfully practiced in other countries, have not been successful in Argentina due to their anti-economic nature.</data>
      <data key="d2">da6bf576b51c96c74aee885ecd44a5d3</data>
      <data key="d5">1</data>
      <data key="d6">68</data>
      <data key="d7">1a5a36eba5d344c9a05b3ff9d0dc23c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOBERAS">
      <data key="d0">NONE</data>
      <data key="d1">Loberas son &#225;reas donde se caza y explota a los lobos marinos, especie de mam&#237;feros marinos adaptados a la vida en el agua y en tierra.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b0c9bb6d4825c2ef5d5962d8392aad5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">69</data>
      <data key="d7">ae1bd745d59f4db29d4d47ae4b7e99f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ACEITE DE LOBO MARINO">
      <data key="d0">PINNIPED</data>
      <data key="d1"> The aceite de lobo marino is a yellow-amber liquid with a distinctive smell of lobo, which solidifies below 0 degrees Celsius, has a variable density ranging from 0.913 to 0.927, and a saponification range of 178 to 196, with an average of 184 to 193. The iodine index is also variable, with an average of 140 to 155. The free acidity and density are low and variable depending on the type of aceite obtained. The extraction methods are diverse, resulting in different types of aceite of varying quality. The aceite de lobo marino is a product obtained from the carne of the lobos marinos, a species of pinn&#237;pedos found in the Atlantic and Fueguina coasts.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b0c9bb6d4825c2ef5d5962d8392aad5,db8b432a978f4e34703f337510f8573d</data>
      <data key="d5">3</data>
      <data key="d6">70</data>
      <data key="d7">1cfa47da298a4e3e82910cf545400a64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORTES">
      <data key="d0">PINNIPED</data>
      <data key="d1">Los cortes son las partes de la carne de los lobos marinos que se separan de la piel y el hueso, y se utilizan para la elaboraci&#243;n del aceite de lobo marino.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b0c9bb6d4825c2ef5d5962d8392aad5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">71</data>
      <data key="d7">6deaa3000f914a1dbf3b7888ca92720f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARREO">
      <data key="d0">PINNIPED</data>
      <data key="d1">El arreo es el proceso de separar a los lobos marinos de la piel y el hueso, y se utiliza para la elaboraci&#243;n del aceite de lobo marino.</data>
      <data key="d2">5b0c9bb6d4825c2ef5d5962d8392aad5</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">72</data>
      <data key="d7">cb46eb91b679418bbcea18dfdfc39efe</data>
    </node>
